# Action positions of any size work: `(p 1 11 10)` over eleven elements
# picks elements 1, 11 and 10.
#
# Today: positions are read as one digit, so `11` and `10` both become
# element 1 and the action silently compiles to `pass[1], pass[1], pass[1]`.
# (architecture.md Appendix A: tendigit.grammar; SPEC §3.2)

@lexer
tokens
    ident
    eof
    err
[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*                      → ident
.                                           → err

@parser
@lang = "ten_positions"

top! = IDENT IDENT IDENT IDENT IDENT IDENT IDENT IDENT IDENT IDENT IDENT → (p 1 11 10)
